1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:02,840
(Leonard:)How come it's not a party
when we do it here?

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:04,540
(Sheldon:)Because we don't
throw parties.

3
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:06,550
(Leonard:)I don't know
what to tell you, Sheldon.

4
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:08,360
(Leonard:)I'm going to see Priya.
Everyone's over there.

5
00:00:08,370 --> 00:00:09,480
(Leonard:)You coming or not?

6
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:11,670
(Sheldon:)Well, no, sir,
and do you know why?

7
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:13,690
In a word: tradition.

8
00:00:13,690 --> 00:00:17,390
(Sheldon:)Every Thursday night
for the last eight years,

9
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:20,040
(Sheldon:)you and I and our friends
have gathered here

10
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:24,030
(Sheldon:)in this very spot to break bread
covered with cheese and sauce,

11
00:00:24,030 --> 00:00:26,170
(Sheldon:)discuss the issues
of the day,

12
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:28,430
(Sheldon:)and yes, share a laugh or two.

13
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:32,340
(Sheldon:)But I guess our rich heritage
means nothing to you.

14
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,540
(Leonard:)I guess you're right.

15
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:34,840
(Leonard:)- See you later.
- Wait!

16
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,640
(Sheldon:)Leonard! Wait!

17
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,540
(Sheldon:)What am I going
to do for dinner?

18
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:40,650
(Leonard:)Come with me to Raj's
and eat there.

19
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:41,950
(Sheldon:)I can't do that.

20
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:45,150
(Sheldon:)What if he serves haggis
and blood pudding?

21
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:48,990
(Leonard:)I really doubt
that's what he'll serve.

22
00:00:48,990 --> 00:00:50,560
(Sheldon:)But what if he does?

23
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,860
(Sheldon:)I'll be obliged to dine

24
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:54,360
(Sheldon:)on liver and lungs stuffed
in a sheep's stomach.

25
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:57,130
(Sheldon:)And frankly, blood pudding is
essentially the same thing.

26
00:00:57,130 --> 00:00:59,330
(Sheldon:)I don't know why
he's serving both.

27
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:00,670
(Leonard:)What do you want to do?

28
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:03,270
(Leonard:)You want to come with me, or
do you want to sit here alone?

29
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:05,200
(Sheldon:)No, I'll go
to your haggis party.

30
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:06,920
(Sheldon:)But I'm telling you.

31
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:11,310
This is adness. This is utter
and complete adness.

32
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:14,930
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

